  "text": "A: So, have you decided on the movie yet?\n\nB: Not really. I was thinking maybe something new, but I feel like I'm running out of options. What did you have in mind?\n\nA: I was just about to ask you the same thing. I\u2019ve been wanting to see that sci-fi one that came out last week.\n\nB: Oh, the one with the time loops? I thought that was *so* overrated.\n\nA: Well, I thought the acting was pretty solid. But I guess everyone has different tastes.\n\nB: Definitely. I prefer the ones with more drama. Or maybe some comedy. I just need to stop watching the same genre every week.\n\nA: That\u2019s fair. I guess I\u2019ve been stuck on action films for a while. It\u2019s kind of boring, honestly.\n\nB: I get that. But I swear, if I watch one more superhero movie, I\u2019m going to start a cult.\n\nA: That\u2019s not so far from what I heard at the theater last night. Someone was seriously proposing a superhero cult.\n\nB: Really? That\u2019s a new one.\n\nA: Yeah, and they were serious about it too. Said they wanted to \"end the world with style.\"\n\nB: That sounds like a plot from a movie.\n\nA: Exactly. So maybe I should just go with something weird instead.\n\nB: I think I\u2019ll go with that. It\u2019s better than pretending I like what I don\u2019t.\n\nA: Fair enough. I\u2019ll go with the time loop movie. Just to see what all the fuss is about.\n\nB: Deal. But if I start crying halfway through, I\u2019m blaming you.\n\nA: No way. That\u2019s on you.",
